                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} monoidal (∞,1)-category
                      %ul
                        %li
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+double+category"} compact double category
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_terms_of_categories_of_modules_and_tensor_product_of_algebras"} In terms of categories of modules and tensor product of algebras
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            operation on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+abelian+category"} finite abelian categories
            is known as the
            %em Deligne tensor product
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %em Deligne box product
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Deligne"} Deligne 90
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊠
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \boxtimes B
            is the abelian category such that for any other abelian category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functors"} exact functors
            of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊠
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \boxtimes B \to C
            are equivalent to functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times B \to C
            that are right exact in each argument separately.
          %p
            This tensor product exists for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+abelian+categories"} finite abelian categories
            but not generally on all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+colimits"} finite colimits
            %a{:href => "#Franco12"} Franco 12
            and (
            %a{:href => "#ChirvasituJohnson-Freyd11"}> Chirvasitu&amp;Johnson-Freyd 11, remark 2.2.8
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#in_terms_of_categories_of_modules_and_tensor_product_of_algebras In terms of categories of modules and tensor product of algebras
          %p
            Recall that for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+abelian+category"} finite abelian category
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            and a
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi fd
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{C} \simeq A Mod_{fd}
                  \\,
          %p
            where the right side consists of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is uniquely determined up to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalence
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B \in Alg_k
              two finite-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebras"} associative algebras
              over a field
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+algebras"} tensor product of algebras
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes_k B
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi fd
                    %mo ⊠
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi fd
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi fd
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A Mod_{fd}
                    \\boxtimes
                    B Mod_{fd}
                    \\simeq
                    (A \otimes_k B) Mod_{fd}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#EGNO"}> EGNO, prop. 1.46.2
            ). Without the finiteness constraints and using the tensor product of categories with finite colimits, this appears as (
            %a{:href => "#ChirvasituJohnson-Freyd11"}> Chirvasitu&amp;Johnson-Freyd 11, remark 2.2.8
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} tensor product of presentable (infinity,1)-categories
          %h2#references References
          %p The construction was introduced in
          %ul#Deligne
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Catégories tannakiennes
          %p
            Ignacio López Franco has pointed out that while Deligne’s tensor product always exists for finite abelian categories, it does not always exist for general
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
          %ul#Franco12
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  Ignacio López Franco
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Ignacio+L%26"} ?
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tensor products of finitely cocomplete and abelian categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0021869313004626"} web
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  Ignacio López Franco
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Ignacio+L%26"} ?
                ,
                %em Tensor products of finitely cococomplete and abelian categories
                (2012) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.mat.uc.pt/~workCT/slides/Ignacio.pdf"}> pdf of slides
                )
          %p Kelly’s tensor product can be found in section 6.5 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Basic concepts of enriched category theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 64
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/10/tr10abs.html"} tac
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/10/tr10.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Similar remarks (in the context of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-rings"} 2-rings
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-modules"} 2-modules
          %ul#ChirvasituJohnson-Freyd11
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandru+Chirvasitu"}> Alexandru Chirvasitu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theo+Johnson-Freyd"} Theo Johnson-Freyd
              = succeed "," do
                %em The fundamental pro-groupoid of an affine 2-scheme
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s10485-011-9275-y"} DOI
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1105.3104"} arXiv:1105.3104
          %p In this set of lecture notes
          %ul#EGNO
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Etingof"}> Pavel Etingof
              , Shlomo Gelaki, Dmitri Nikshych,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ostrik"} Victor Ostrik
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topics in Lie theory and Tensor Categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://ocw.mit.edu/courses/mathematics/18-769-topics-in-lie-theory-tensor-categories-spring-2009/lecture-notes/"} web
          %p
            the Deligne tensor product is discussed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://ocw.mit.edu/courses/mathematics/18-769-topics-in-lie-theory-tensor-categories-spring-2009/lecture-notes/MIT18_769S09_lec09.pdf"} lecture 9
